<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberating Expedition of Peru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1820">1820</a>–<a href="/years/1821">1821</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peruvian-war-of-independence">Peruvian War of Independence</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liberating Expedition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> was the military campaign led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a> from Chile against the royalist stronghold of Peru. Carried by a Chilean fleet under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-cochrane-10th-earl-of-dundonald">Thomas Cochrane</a>, it sailed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valparaiso">Valparaíso</a> in August 1820 and landed near Pisco. The royalists abandoned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 1821, and San Martín proclaimed the independence of Peru on 28 July 1821.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberating-expedition-of-peru.jpg" alt="Liberating Expedition of Peru" width="320" height="259" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernardo O'Higgins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:El_Batall%C3%B3n_Numancia_recibe_la_Bandera_del_Ej%C3%A9rcito_Libertador.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
